  "subject": "a young man who orders a bowl of the bitterest twenty-four-herb tea every day at a herbal tea shop just to keep talking to the girl at the counter, until she tells him to stop drinking and shares a honey tea instead",
  "caption": "Cantonese opera-film song pop in the 1960s Hong Kong cinema style, built on a lively siu kuk folk tune. Gaohu carrying the melody with slides, yangqin strummed in bright tremolo runs, small Chinese drum and wooden clappers marking a bouncy two-beat, upright bass walking, brushed snare. Warm vintage studio room, slight tape warmth. Male tenor with bright forward tone, light operatic ornaments but plain sung words, playful comic delivery. Clear full voice, every word enunciated, steady sung melody on every line. 112 BPM, D major. Playful, cheeky, lovestruck. No electric guitar, no synth, no drum machine, no autotune, no rap, no heavy gongs.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n廿四味，一碗黑，濃到似墨水\n阿強入嚟坐低，面都唔變色\n老闆個女話：「先生，好苦㗎」\n佢笑笑口講：「我最鍾意苦」\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n一啖落肚，條脷縮埋\n點都要撐住，唔可以皺眉\n\n[Chorus]\n苦又苦，我照飲晒佢\n只因你喺櫃枱後面望住我\n苦又苦，我再叫多碗\n你一笑，我就覺得有啲甜\n\n[Verse]\n今日轉試夏枯草，仲要加蒲公英\n個胃喺度打鼓，好似開鑼\n你拎碟陳皮梅，偷偷哋放低\n我話唔使喇，其實想再坐多陣\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n伙記話我腸胃，真係無敵\n佢哋唔知，我係咬緊牙關\n\n[Chorus]\n苦又苦，我照飲晒佢\n只因你喺櫃枱後面望住我\n苦又苦，我再叫多碗\n你一笑，我就覺得有啲甜\n\n[Verse]\n成個月，我飲咗三十碗\n個個街坊都話我好有胃口\n你終於放低茶壺：「喂，夠喇」\n\n[Bridge]\n「你唔使飲，我都知你想傾偈」\n「由第一碗，我就睇出嚟」\n\n[Chorus]\n苦完又苦，我今日唔飲\n你斟碗蜜糖茶，一人一半\n苦完又苦，我都值得\n呢碗最甜，係你遞過嚟\n\n[Chorus]\n苦完又苦，我今日唔飲\n你斟碗蜜糖茶，一人一半\n苦完又苦，我都值得\n呢碗最甜，係你遞過嚟\n\n[Outro]\n廿四味，夠喇夠喇\n今日飲，蜜糖水",
